# Example only. Copy and adapt outside the repository before installing.
# Do NOT embed GitHub tokens, SSH keys, API keys, or other secrets here.
# Credentials come from the cron user's existing environment (gh auth, SSH).
#
# V1 execution tick (SPEC §47.2): one run of scripts/run_parallel_scheduler_tick.py.
# It reaps stale runtime, releases or stops dependencies, then starts eligible
# Tickets up to the free max_concurrent_tasks capacity, and exits. It never
# integrates (SPEC §47.4). Nothing here is installed: installing or changing a
# cron entry is a human operator action (SPEC §47.4).
#
# Replace every {{PLACEHOLDER}} with an absolute path before installing:
#   {{PYTHON}}         the Python of the deployed checkout's environment
#   {{TASKFLOW_HOME}}  the deployed agent-taskflow checkout (deployment target: human decision H2)
#   {{DB}}             the Taskflow SQLite state database (explicit; there is no default)
#   {{LOG_DIR}}        an existing, writable log directory
#
# Non-overlap (SPEC §47.3): the tick holds its own flock on
# {{DB}}.execution-tick.lock for its whole run. An overlapping invocation, from
# cron or by hand, appends one {"status": "skipped_overlap", ...} line to the
# JSONL log and exits 75 without doing any work. Do NOT also wrap this line in
# flock(1) on that same file: the tick would then contend with its own wrapper
# and skip every run. Do not add timeout(1) either: a skip that repeats is the
# visible signal that the cadence is wrong or a run is stuck.
#
# Exit codes: 0 ran, 2 missing migration (message in the stderr log) or a lock
# that cannot be taken (one error JSON line in the log), 75 skipped_overlap.
#
# HUMAN CHOICE: by default the tick waits for its workers, so the lock is held
# until they finish. Append --no-wait to return once every started Ticket is
# claimed; workers keep running and the next tick may start more work.
#
# Cadence: every 5 minutes. Provisional (SPEC §47.2); revisit after the first
# real Ticket runs.
#
# How to disable: comment out or remove the line below with `crontab -e`.

PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

*/5 * * * * "{{PYTHON}}" "{{TASKFLOW_HOME}}/scripts/run_parallel_scheduler_tick.py" --db-path "{{DB}}" --jsonl >> "{{LOG_DIR}}/execution-tick.jsonl" 2>> "{{LOG_DIR}}/execution-tick.stderr.log"
